# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the cpp-sanitize CI job (doc/fuzzing.md).
#
# Only leaks inside third-party libraries belong here, one `leak:<symbol or
# library>` line each, with the reason. A leak in meshio++'s own code is a bug
# to fix, never a line in this file.

# netCDF-4's `nc_open` leaks what it had allocated (the object-header buffer of
# `H5Gopen2` and the variable hash map) when it fails halfway through a corrupt
# file, as the committed fuzz input tests/fuzz/regressions/ugrid_nc makes it do.
# The leak is inside libnetcdf/libhdf5 with no meshio++ frame, and only stacks
# through `NC_open` are matched (the instrumented fuzz campaign's twin is
# tools/fuzz/lsan_libraries.supp).
leak:NC_open
